+`a[i]`, but implemented so that the element's reference count is *not* read when the element is an
+object of a memory-mapped compacted region (`lean_array_fget_no_touch`, `src/runtime/object.cpp`).
+
+Objects in compacted regions are persistent (`rc = 0`); `inc`/`dec` on them are no-ops whose only
+effect is to read the object header, i.e. to fault in the page of the `.olean` file that holds the
+object. `finalizeImport` only *stores* the `ConstantInfo` pointers of the imported modules into the
+constant maps, so with the ordinary `a[i]` (which increments the reference count of the returned
+element) a `import Mathlib` touches the page of every one of ~770k `ConstantInfo` objects, scattered
+over the whole ~7 GB of mapped files, although no proof or type is ever looked at. This primitive
+checks membership in a compacted region by address (the loader registers the address ranges it maps
+regions into) and skips the increment in that case; for every other element it behaves exactly like
+`a[i]`. The result is owned, as with `a[i]`.
