+/-!
+### Process-persistent cache of computed entries
+
+For modules built without stored entries (e.g. a Mathlib built by a toolchain without this
+extension), the entries computed by the first walk of a process can be cached on disk
+(`LEAN_SEARCH_INDEX_CACHE_DIR`, one file per import closure, keyed by the module names and the `.olean`
+sizes/mtimes) and are then used like stored entries by every later process (file workers of the
+language server included). The per-module entry lists are derived from the finished
+`PreDiscrTree`: for every root key its entry array is traversed in order and each entry appended
+to its module's list, so re-inserting the lists module by module rebuilds every root array in the
+same order.
+-/
+
+/-- Cached index entries, one array per `ModuleIdx`. -/
+structure IndexCache where
+  mods : Array (Array IndexEntry)
+
+private def searchIndexCacheVersion : UInt64 := 2
